.\" help2man include for imud-mavlink.8 — the hand-written sections.
.\" OPTIONS is generated from `imud-mavlink --help`; everything else lives here.
.\" See tools/man-postprocess.py and `make docs-man`.

[NAME]
imud\-mavlink \- bridge imud's binary stream to MAVLink over UDP/serial/TCP

[SYNOPSIS]
.B imud-mavlink
\&[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
\&[\fB\-\-version\fR]

[DESCRIPTION]
.B imud-mavlink
connects to the local AF_UNIX binary subscription stream published by
.BR imud (8)
and emits MAVLink for ArduPilot, PX4, or a ground station (QGroundControl,
Mission Planner).  It sends
.B HEARTBEAT
(#0) at 1 Hz and, at
.IR rate_hz ,
.B ATTITUDE
(#30) and/or
.B ATTITUDE_QUATERNION
(#31).  MAVLink protocol version 1 or 2 is selectable.
.PP
The bridge is pure C (a hand-rolled encoder, no external dependencies).
MAVLink's body frame is FRD/NED \(em the same as imud \(em so roll/pitch/yaw,
the gyro body rates, and the quaternion pass through directly
(SI radians / rad/s).  It reads the stream socket named by its own
.B socket
key (default
.IR /run/imud/imud-stream.sock ),
so
.BR imud (8)
must have its
.B [stream]
output enabled, and it reconnects automatically if imud restarts.
.PP
Output goes to
.BR UDP ,
.BR serial ,
and/or a
.B TCP listener
simultaneously (each independently enabled).  Serial is opened raw, 8N1, at the
configured baud; the shipped unit grants the service the
.B dialout
group and tty-device access.  With
.B tcp_enabled
ground stations connect as TCP clients
.RB ( tcp://<host>:5760
in QGroundControl / Mission Planner) and every connected client receives the
same frames.

[SIGNALS]
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration.  The protocol version, rate, message selection, UDP
destination, and log level are applied live; the system/component ids and which
transports are enabled require a restart.  If the reload fails to parse, the
running configuration is kept.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Graceful shutdown.

[CONFIGURATION]
Read from
.I /etc/imud/imud-mavlink.conf
(the
.B [imud-mavlink]
section); the keys are documented in
.BR imud-mavlink.conf (5).

[FILES]
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud-mavlink.conf
Default configuration file.

[EXAMPLES]
Run against a local ground station on UDP:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
imud-mavlink --config /etc/imud/imud-mavlink.conf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Enable as a service (after enabling imud's
.B [stream]
output and at least one transport \(em
.BR udp_enabled ,\  serial_enabled ,
and/or
.B tcp_enabled
\(em in
.IR imud-mavlink.conf ;
the daemon itself is enabled by default):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo systemctl enable --now imud-mavlink
.EE
.RE

[SEE ALSO]
.BR imud-mavlink.conf (5),
.BR imud (8),
.BR imud-signalk (8),
.BR imud-mqtt (8),
.BR imud-influxdb (8),
.BR imud.conf (5)

